
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Código Penal (Decreto-Lei nº 2.848/1940) — domínio comum: os SUBSTANTIVOS.
--
-- Written by the ontology pass (g0). Read-only to every other encoder: a noun
-- that is missing here is declared in the encoder's own module with a comment
-- `-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: <why>` and listed in its notes; the conductor hoists it.
--
-- WHAT BELONGS HERE. A noun goes in this file only if BOTH hold:
--   1. more than one Título of the Code (or the Parte Geral and a Título)
--      needs it; and
--   2. a witness of ordinary competence could testify to it — a date, a
--      kinship, a weapon, a value — without reading the Code.
-- Whether a set of facts makes out an offence is a RULE, and lives with the
-- article that says so. This file declares types only: no rule, no constant,
-- no directive.
--
-- HOW THE RECORDS ARE MEANT TO BE USED. Each offence module declares its own
-- case record (`Fato de furto`, `Fato de roubo`, ...) that EMBEDS the records
-- below and adds the facts only its article reads. Checkbox facts are LISTS of
-- enumerations, not records of booleans: L4 has no record-update syntax, so a
-- test case would otherwise have to spell out every flag; with a list it names
-- only the circumstances that are present, and an empty list says "none".
-- A list member that is absent means the fact did not occur.
--
-- Two conventions every encoder relies on:
--   * DATES. Ages are never stored: a person has a date of birth, a fact has a
--     date, and `cp-pena.l4` computes the age in completed years at whichever
--     date a provision names (the date of the fact, or of the sentence).
--   * CLASSIFICATIONS THAT BELONG TO A RULE are delegated to the fact supplier
--     only where the practice itself supplies them: the grade of a bodily
--     injury is what the medical report (laudo de exame de corpo de delito)
--     answers, so `Resultado` carries it; art. 129 §§ 1º–2º, which define the
--     grades, are encoded by g2. Fork F-g0-07 records the choice.

§ `Código Penal — domínio comum (substantivos)`

§§ `Pessoa`

-- A natural person, as the parties and witnesses identify them. Time-dependent
-- conditions (pregnancy, disability) are not here: they are facts about the
-- person AT THE TIME OF THE FACT and live on the role records below.
DECLARE Pessoa HAS
    `identificação` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en the identification of the person
    `data de nascimento` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the date of birth
    mulher IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the person is a woman

§§ `Relação do agente com a vítima`

-- What the AGENT is to the VICTIM, in the Code's own words: "se o agente é
-- ascendente ... da vítima" (art. 226, II), "contra ascendente, descendente,
-- irmão ou cônjuge" (art. 61, II, e), "prevalecendo-se de relações domésticas,
-- de coabitação ou de hospitalidade" (art. 61, II, f; art. 129, § 9º). Record
-- every relation that holds: a tutor who is also an uncle is both.
-- Art. 181, II ("seja o parentesco legítimo ou ilegítimo, seja civil ou
-- natural") is why the kinship members carry no such qualifier.
DECLARE `Relação do agente com a vítima` IS ONE OF
    ascendente
    @nlg:en an ascendant of the victim
    descendente
    @nlg:en a descendant of the victim
    irmão
    @nlg:en a sibling of the victim
    cônjuge
    @nlg:en the spouse of the victim
    companheiro
    @nlg:en the partner (companheiro or companheira) of the victim
    `padrasto ou madrasta`
    @nlg:en the stepfather or stepmother of the victim
    enteado
    @nlg:en the stepchild of the victim
    tio
    @nlg:en an uncle or aunt of the victim
    sobrinho
    @nlg:en a nephew or niece of the victim
    tutor
    @nlg:en the guardian (tutor) of the victim
    curador
    @nlg:en the curator of the victim
    preceptor
    @nlg:en the tutor or teacher (preceptor) of the victim
    empregador
    @nlg:en the employer of the victim
    `superior hierárquico`
    @nlg:en the hierarchical superior of the victim in employment, office or function
    `outra relação de autoridade sobre a vítima`
    @nlg:en someone who by any other title has authority over the victim
    `guarda, cuidado ou vigilância da vítima`
    @nlg:en someone under whose care, custody or supervision the victim is
    `obrigação de cuidado, proteção ou vigilância assumida por lei ou outra forma`
    @nlg:en someone who took on, by law or otherwise, a duty of care, protection or supervision over the victim
    `relações domésticas`
    @nlg:en someone in a domestic relationship with the victim
    `coabitação`
    @nlg:en someone living with the victim
    hospitalidade
    @nlg:en the host or guest of the victim
    `relação de trabalho doméstico`
    @nlg:en someone in a domestic-work relationship with the victim
    `convivência atual ou passada`
    @nlg:en someone who lives or has lived with the victim
    `relação íntima de afeto atual ou passada`
    @nlg:en someone in a present or past intimate relationship with the victim

§§ `Condição da vítima na data do fato`

-- Conditions of the victim AT THE TIME OF THE FACT that a witness or an
-- expert can attest. Ages are computed, never listed here (see the header).
DECLARE `Condição da vítima` IS ONE OF
    gestante
    @nlg:en pregnant
    `pessoa com deficiência`
    @nlg:en a person with a disability
    enfermo
    @nlg:en ill
    `sem o necessário discernimento para a prática do ato, por enfermidade ou deficiência mental`
    @nlg:en lacking, through illness or mental disability, the discernment needed for the act
    `sem possibilidade de oferecer resistência, por qualquer outra causa`
    @nlg:en unable, for any other reason, to offer resistance

§§ `Vínculo com a administração pública (art. 327)`

-- The facts art. 327 decides "funcionário público" from. The DEFINITION is
-- art. 327's (g6 encodes it); these are only the facts it reads. The caput's
-- "embora transitoriamente ou sem remuneração" means the first field is TRUE
-- for a transitory or unpaid holder too: the field records the exercise, not
-- its terms.
DECLARE `Vínculo com a administração pública` HAS
    `exerce cargo, emprego ou função pública` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en exercises a public office, post or function, even transitorily or without pay
    `exerce cargo, emprego ou função em entidade paraestatal` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en exercises an office, post or function in a parastatal entity
    `trabalha para empresa contratada ou conveniada para atividade típica da Administração Pública` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en works for a service company contracted or conveniada to carry out an activity typical of the Public Administration
    `ocupa cargo em comissão ou função de direção ou assessoramento` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en holds a commissioned office or a management or advisory function in a body of the direct administration, a mixed-capital company, a public company or a foundation instituted by the public power

§§ `Agente`

-- The groups the Code names since Lei nº 15.358/2026 and before it. Record
-- EVERY description that fits: an "organização criminosa ultraviolenta" is also
-- an "organização criminosa", so an agent in one carries both members — art.
-- 158, § 4º names the plain one, art. 155, § 9º the ultraviolent one.
DECLARE `Grupo criminoso` IS ONE OF
    `organização criminosa`
    @nlg:en a criminal organisation
    `organização criminosa ultraviolenta`
    @nlg:en an ultraviolent criminal organisation
    `grupo paramilitar`
    @nlg:en a paramilitary group
    `milícia privada`
    @nlg:en a private militia

-- `reincidente` is a STATUS read off the criminal record, as the court
-- certifies it; arts. 63–64 decide it and g1 encodes them. It is here because
-- arts. 149-A § 2º, 155 § 2º, 168-A § 3º, 170, 171 § 1º and 337-A § 2º all turn
-- on "primário", which the Code does not define and which this encoding reads
-- as "não reincidente" (fork F-g0-05). g1 can tie the two together with a
-- cross-check assertion at integration (phrasebook entry 1.9).
DECLARE Agente HAS
    pessoa IS A Pessoa
    @nlg:en the person who acted
    reincidente IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the agent is a repeat offender, as the criminal record certifies
    `vínculo com a administração pública` IS A `Vínculo com a administração pública`
    @nlg:en the agent's link with the public administration
    `grupos de que é integrante` IS A LIST OF `Grupo criminoso`
    @nlg:en the criminal groups the agent is a member of

§§ `Vítima`

-- The victim when the victim is a natural person. An offence whose victim may
-- be a legal person or the collectivity holds this in a MAYBE.
DECLARE `Vítima` HAS
    pessoa IS A Pessoa
    @nlg:en the person who suffered the crime
    `condições na data do fato` IS A LIST OF `Condição da vítima`
    @nlg:en the victim's conditions at the time of the fact
    `relações com o agente` IS A LIST OF `Relação do agente com a vítima`
    @nlg:en what the agent is to the victim
    `vínculo com a administração pública` IS A `Vínculo com a administração pública`
    @nlg:en the victim's link with the public administration

§§ `Coisa`

-- A thing, as its owner, holder or an appraiser would describe it. The
-- categories only Título II names (cellphone, livestock, fuel ...) are g3's and
-- live in g3's modules; `veículo automotor` is here because Títulos II and X
-- both turn on it (arts. 155 § 5º, 157 § 2º IV, 311).
DECLARE Coisa HAS
    `descrição` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en the description of the thing
    `móvel` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the thing is movable
    alheia IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the thing belongs to someone other than the agent
    `valor em reais` IS A NUMBER
    @nlg:en the economic value of the thing in reais at the time of the fact
    `veículo automotor` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the thing is a motor vehicle

§§ `Documento`

-- A document, as the one who holds it would describe it. What makes a paper
-- a "documento público" for penal purposes, and what is equated to one, is
-- art. 297's to decide (g5); `público` records how the document presents
-- itself — issued by a public authority, or not.
DECLARE Documento HAS
    `descrição` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en the description of the document
    `público` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the document is a public document
    verdadeiro IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the document is genuine

§§ `Meio empregado`

-- How the act was carried out, in the Code's words. A weapon is recorded by
-- its kind: "arma de fogo" in the Code (arts. 157 § 2º-A, 155 § 7º) is either
-- firearm member; "arma de fogo de uso restrito ou proibido" (arts. 121 § 2º
-- VIII, 157 § 2º-B) is only the second; "arma", unqualified (arts. 146 § 1º,
-- 147-A, 150 § 1º, 158 § 1º), is any of the weapon members — which of them
-- counts is each group's fork to record.
DECLARE `Meio empregado` IS ONE OF
    `violência à pessoa`
    @nlg:en violence against a person
    `grave ameaça`
    @nlg:en a serious threat
    `ameaça`
    @nlg:en a threat
    fraude
    @nlg:en fraud
    `redução da vítima à impossibilidade de resistência, por qualquer meio`
    @nlg:en reducing the victim, by any means, to being unable to resist
    `violência contra coisa`
    @nlg:en violence against a thing
    `emprego de arma branca`
    @nlg:en the use of a bladed or other non-firearm weapon (arma branca)
    `emprego de arma de fogo de uso permitido`
    @nlg:en the use of a firearm of permitted use
    `emprego de arma de fogo de uso restrito ou proibido`
    @nlg:en the use of a firearm of restricted or prohibited use
    `emprego de outro objeto como arma`
    @nlg:en the use of another object as a weapon
    `emprego de explosivo ou de artefato análogo que cause perigo comum`
    @nlg:en the use of an explosive or a similar device causing common danger
    veneno
    @nlg:en poison
    fogo
    @nlg:en fire
    asfixia
    @nlg:en asphyxia
    tortura
    @nlg:en torture
    `traição`
    @nlg:en treachery
    emboscada
    @nlg:en ambush
    `dissimulação`
    @nlg:en dissimulation
    `paga ou promessa de recompensa`
    @nlg:en payment or the promise of a reward

§§ `Resultado`

-- The grade of each injury as the medical report classifies it (see the
-- header and fork F-g0-07). Record one member per result that occurred to
-- anyone; an empty list means no one was hurt.
DECLARE Resultado IS ONE OF
    `lesão corporal`
    @nlg:en bodily injury
    `lesão corporal de natureza grave`
    @nlg:en serious bodily injury (art. 129, § 1º)
    `lesão corporal de natureza gravíssima`
    @nlg:en very serious bodily injury (art. 129, § 2º)
    morte
    @nlg:en death

§§ `Circunstâncias do fato`

-- Circumstances of time, place and context that more than one Título names.
-- Circumstances only one article or Título names (the "repouso noturno" of
-- art. 155 § 1º, the "lugar ermo" of arts. 133 and 150) belong to that module.
DECLARE `Circunstância do fato` IS ONE OF
    `no território nacional`
    @nlg:en in the national territory
    `nas dependências de instituição de ensino`
    @nlg:en on the premises of an educational institution
    `em ocasião de incêndio, naufrágio, inundação ou calamidade pública`
    @nlg:en during a fire, shipwreck, flood or public calamity
    `no exercício da função pública`
    @nlg:en in the exercise of a public function
    `em razão da função pública`
    @nlg:en because of a public function
    `a pretexto de exercer a função pública`
    @nlg:en under the pretext of exercising a public function
    `prevalecendo-se do cargo`
    @nlg:en taking advantage of a public office
    `em descumprimento de medida protetiva de urgência`
    @nlg:en in breach of an urgent protective measure
    `no contexto das condutas do art. 2º do marco legal do combate ao crime organizado`
    @nlg:en in the context of, or to achieve, the conduct in art. 2 of the law instituting the legal framework for combating organised crime in Brazil

§§ `Fato`

-- The facts of the act itself that every Título shares. An offence module's
-- case record embeds one of these.
DECLARE Fato HAS
    `data do fato` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the date of the act (art. 4: the moment of the action or omission)
    `número de pessoas que concorreram para o crime` IS A NUMBER
    @nlg:en the number of people, the agent included, who took part in the crime
    `meios empregados` IS A LIST OF `Meio empregado`
    @nlg:en the means used
    resultados IS A LIST OF Resultado
    @nlg:en the injuries or deaths that resulted
    `circunstâncias` IS A LIST OF `Circunstância do fato`
    @nlg:en the circumstances of time, place and context

§§ `Elemento subjetivo (art. 18)`

-- Hoisted at integration (integ-shared, 2026-09-30) from cp-g2a-comum and
-- cp-g4b-comum, whose declarations were the same two members; the glosses are
-- g4b's. Both marked it PROPOSTO-COMUM: every Título with a culpable form
-- needs it (arts. 121 § 3º, 129 § 6º, 180 § 3º, 250–285, 312 § 2º,
-- 351 § 4º ...). Whether the agent acted with dolo or with culpa is the
-- court's finding on the evidence (art. 18), supplied as input.
-- g1a's art. 18 reads the finer facts behind this finding (whether the agent
-- wanted the result, took on its risk, or caused it by imprudência,
-- negligência or imperícia) as `Relação do agente com o resultado`, in
-- cp-g1a-crime; tying the two together is a later wiring pass.
DECLARE `Elemento subjetivo` IS ONE OF
    dolo
    @nlg:en intent (dolo): the agent wanted the result or took the risk of producing it
    culpa
    @nlg:en fault (culpa): the agent caused the result through imprudence, negligence or lack of skill

§§ `Execução do crime (art. 14)`

-- Hoisted at integration (integ-shared, 2026-09-30) from cp-g2b-comum
-- (`Execução do crime`) and cp-g6b-comum (`Execução`), whose declarations
-- were the same two fields. They are the two facts about the execution that
-- cp-pena's `crime tentado (art. 14, II)` reads beside the elements of the
-- crime, which each offence decides for itself. `execução iniciada` is TRUE
-- for a consummated crime too.
-- Other groups record how far the execution went differently, and are not
-- (yet) this type: g1a's `Curso da execução` (cp-g1a-crime, with art. 17's
-- facts), and the four-member enums `Etapa da execução` (cp-g3b-comum) and
-- `Estágio da execução` (cp-g5-comum, cp-g6a-casos); notes/integration.md.
DECLARE `Execução do crime` HAS
    `execução iniciada` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the agent began to carry out the crime
    `consumação impedida por circunstâncias alheias à vontade do agente` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en something outside the agent's will stopped the crime from being completed
